  "description": "AT END on a sequential READ - FILE STATUS '10', which app/cbl/CBSTM03A.CBL:353-359 turns into MOVE 'Y' TO END-OF-FILE. One record is seeded, so the second READ reaches the end of the file. The caller deliberately does NOT issue MOVE SPACES TO WS-M03B-FLDT before that second read - the pattern at app/cbl/CBSTM03A.CBL:857-860, which clears the status but not the area - so the expectation can state the thing that is easy to get wrong: at end of file the record area is returned UNCHANGED and therefore still holds the record the previous READ delivered. A translation that blanked the area on end of file would pass every status assertion and fail this one.",
